{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "type": "how-to",
  "title": "How to test a service from start to exit code without a process",
  "problem": "I want specs for how my service boots, stops and exits, but the only way I know to test that is to spawn it, wait for its port, send it a signal and read its exit code, which is slow and depends on timing, and a service I run inside the test process instead ends the test runner when it exits.",
  "outcome": "Specs that run the service definition over a fake process and assert its lines and its exit code for a refused environment, a start, a stop that was asked for, a failed start, a fault and a timeout, and specs that call its steps as functions, all in milliseconds with no port bound and no signal sent, in a run that exits by itself.",
  "priority": "P1",
